ht="1.934ex" role="img" focusable="false" viewBox="0 -705 2714.6 855" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"><g stroke="currentColor" fill="currentColor" stroke-width="0" transform="scale(1,-1)"><g data-mml-node="math"><g data-mml-node="msub"><g data-mml-node="TeXAtom" data-mjx-texclass="ORD"><g data-mml-node="mi"><use data-c="48" xlink:href="#MJX-TEX-N-48"></use><use data-c="4E" xlink:href="#MJX-TEX-N-4E" transform="translate(750,0)"></use><use data-c="4F" xlink:href="#MJX-TEX-N-4F" transform="translate(1500,0)"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node="mn" transform="translate(2311,-150) scale(0.707)"><use data-c="32" xlink:href="#MJX-TEX-N-32"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> can also be used for the diazotization reaction <div></div>The reaction involves the formation of nitrosonium ion ( <mjx-container class="MathJax" jax="SVG" overflow="overflow"><svg style="vertical-align: -0.05ex;" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="4.889ex" height="1.96ex" role="img" focusable="false" viewBox="0 -844.3 2161.1 866.3" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"><g stroke="currentColor" fill="currentColor" stroke-width="0" transform="scale(1,-1)"><g data-mml-node="math"><g data-mml-node="msup"><g data-mml-node="TeXAtom" data-mjx-texclass="ORD"><g data-mml-node="mi"><use data-c="4E" xlink:href="#MJX-TEX-N-4E"></use><use data-c="4F" xlink:href="#MJX-TEX-N-4F" transform="translate(750,0)"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node="TeXAtom" transform="translate(1561,432.1) scale(0.707)" data-mjx-texclass="ORD"><g data-mml-node="mo"><use data-c="2B" xlink:href="#MJX-TEX-N-2B"></use></g></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>) which attacks the aromatic ring, leading to the formation of diazonium salt.
